# Output of the admin scripts in scripts/. These are local review artifacts
# containing raw GitHub API responses (collaborator lists, protection state).
# Nothing secret, but it is point-in-time output that goes stale immediately —
# the verification transcript belongs in the pull request, not in the tree.
scripts/protection-result.txt
scripts/environments-result.txt

# Go.gov exports used as reference while building the reconciliation importer.
#
# NOT COMMITTED. @clolry's monthly exports carry ~400 real GSA traveler names
# and 391 real employee IDs each. Finding G-056 already flags six real
# employees' addresses sitting in test fixtures as a problem; adding 800 more
# names to git history would be a larger instance of the same thing, and
# history is not something you can take back.
#
# The importer's test suite reads them from /tmp when present and SKIPS its
# measured-numbers section when absent, so a fresh checkout still passes.
#
# To re-run the measured assertions locally, convert the .xls files to JSON at
# /tmp/opencode/req.json and /tmp/opencode/exp.json — see
# test_gogov_sync.js §8.
reference_excel_files/report_*.xls
reference_excel_files/Expense Report*.xls
reference_excel_files/Travel requests*.xls

# The ASD staffing plan: 806 named staff with position numbers, titles and
# duty stations. Same reasoning as above, and more of it.
reference_excel_files/*Staffing Plan*.xlsx

# The ASD FY27 Travel/Liability Log: named travelers, routes, dates and
# dollar amounts for 30 real trips. @clolry shares it locally so the importer
# can be written against the real column shapes; it must not be committed.
#
# LiabilityLogSync.js reads it from the spreadsheet named in the
# LIABILITY_LOG_SHEET_ID script property, never from this folder — and
# test_hc_roster_import.js §7 fails the build if any server file references
# this directory at all.
reference_excel_files/*Travel_Liability Log*.xlsx

# Chiquita's reconciliation workbook, the source for the existing-travel
# importer.
#
# NOT COMMITTED, same reasoning as the Go.gov exports above and more of it.
# This one carries MORE real personal data than either: ~1,900 traveler
# names across its two source tabs, 823 real GSA email addresses and 823
# supervisor names in FasData, and 274 employee IDs. Finding G-056 flags six
# real employees' addresses in test fixtures as a problem; this would be a far
# larger instance, and git history is not something you can take back.
#
# test_travel_import.js §21 reads a JSON conversion from /tmp when present and
# SKIPS its measured section when absent, so a fresh checkout still passes.
# The conversion format is documented in docs/DEPLOYMENT_TRAVEL_IMPORT.md §6.
#
# Matched anywhere in the tree, not just at the root, because it arrived at
# the repository root rather than in reference_excel_files/.
*Expense Report Calculations*.xlsx
*Expense Report Calculations*.xls